## Full analysis scripts

The anlyses for this paper were done in brms: https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/pdf/10.1177/20416695221109300
scripts are on OSF (link in the paper)

Drift-diffusion model analysis in brms: https://github.com/mdllz/con-diffusion
The analyses are integrated into the RMarkdown manuscript

## Equivalence testing

Why maybe not do it: https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Richard-Morey/publication/51519224_Bayes_Factor_Approaches_for_Testing_Interval_Null_Hypotheses/links/0fcfd50f05f1be35d2000000/Bayes-Factor-Approaches-for-Testing-Interval-Null-Hypotheses.pdf

But also what is ROPE: https://easystats.github.io/bayestestR/articles/region_of_practical_equivalence.html
